 "text": "Hey, how's your day been so far? They usually charge around per hour, and some will do a flat fee for a wedding of that size. That's where a plan comes in. It holds everyone to deadlines, so nobody's chasing their noses. It means the big day is the next day. Everything needs to be set up by the evening before, so the couple can rest. It is, if you start early. Many couples book a year in advance. Maybe she'd help in exchange for a good chair in the kitchen. Planners love that.",
